 God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙĞBut all that heard him were amazed, and said; Is not this he that destroyed them which called on this name in Jerusalem, and came hither for that intent, that he might bring them bound unto the chief priests?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{But Saul increased the more in strength, and confounded the Jews which dwelt at Damascus, proving that this is very Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKAnd after that many days were fulfilled, the Jews took counsel to kill him:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_but their laying await was known of Saul. And they watched the gates day and night to kill him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOThen the disciples took him by night, and let him down by the wall in a basket.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And when Saul was come to Jerusalem, he assayed to join himself to the disciples: but they were all afraid of him, and believed not that he was a disciple.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÓBut Barnabas took him, and brought him to the apostles, and declared unto them how he had seen the Lord in the way, and that he had spoken to him, and how he had preached boldly at Damascus in the name of Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:And he was with them coming in and going out at Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd he spake boldly in the name of the Lord Jesus, and disputed against the Grecians: but they went about to slay him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Which when the brethren knew, they brought him down to CÃ¦sarea, and sent him forth to Tarsus.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·Then had the churches rest throughout all JudÃ¦a and Galilee and Samaria, and were edified; and walking in the fear of the Lord, and in the comfort of the Holy Ghost, were multiplied.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter	«first_verse ªlast_verse#¦verses”„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd it came to pass, as Peter passed throughout all quarters, he came down also to the saints which dwelt at Lydda.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd there he found a certain man named Ã†neas, which had kept his bed eight years, and was sick of the palsy.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd Peter said unto him, Ã†neas, Jesus Christ maketh thee whole: arise, and make thy bed. And he arose immediately.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFAnd all that dwelt at Lydda and Saron saw him, and turned to the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book+§chapter	«first_verse$ªlast_verse+¦verses˜„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡Now there was at Joppa a certain disciple named Tabitha, which by interpretation is called Dorcas: this woman was full of good works and almsdeeds which she did.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}And it came to pass in those days, that she was sick, and died: whom when they had washed, they laid her in an upper chamber.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­And forasmuch as Lydda was nigh to Joppa, and the disciples had heard that Peter was there, they sent unto him two men, desiring him that he would not delay to come to them.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ×Then Peter arose and went with them. When he was come, they brought him into the upper chamber: and all the widows stood by him weeping, and shewing the coats and garments which Dorcas made, while she was with them.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªBut Peter put them all forth, and kneeled down, and prayed; and turning him to the body said, Tabitha, arise. And she opened her eyes: and when she saw Peter, she sat up.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd he gave her his hand, and lifted her up, and when he had called the saints and widows, presented her alive.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEAnd it was known throughout all Joppa; and many believed in the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPAnd it came to pass, that he tarried many days in Joppa with one Simon a tanner.¦layout ªlast_verse+